    "name": "Bioysque",
    "steam_appid": 2384020,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2384020/extras/aa5e9eb451fb97f592759f5229e06a62.avif?t=1749786548\" /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>OVERVIEW:</i></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bioysque is a retro-style Action RPG in a dark bio-horror environment, both sci-fi and fantasy motives. You are always alone and they are always many. Fight surreal creatures, get experience, explore and gather upgrades - get stronger before the next big Boss fight, learn the truth. Win and be rewarded.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>DEVELOPER'S MESSAGE:</i></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I never intended to make this game. But I saw it in a dream, so I had to make it! For some strange reason, that's pretty rare for me. I have seen about 3 dreams in my whole life (or more likely, those are all I remember). I had to try at least. (<strong><i>time skip here</i></strong>) And here it is. I actually made the game I saw in a dream. What could be more surreal than that?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2384020/extras/5fa19cc563e1e69b035bf57057b282b4.avif?t=1749786548\" /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>3 MOST IMPORTANT FEATURES:</i></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rare - <i>forgotten/unknown</i> - Biopunk Sci-Fi/Fantasy setting; short but multi-layered story</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unique &lt;direct click&gt; battle system: no time wasted! Hit whatever you see wherever it is!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Mostly Wall-less level design and portal-based world. <i>*more about it in the section below...</i></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2384020/extras/ba675d8106948968ebbac7a9dc99a757.webp?t=1749786548\" /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>WARNING I:</i></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Exploration done differently, and I think it's preferable to know, before you try the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2384020/extras/aded8ff0726c28639613ce4910842132.avif?t=1749786548\" /></span></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >| Most rooms/locations are connected via portals. </p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >| You always start in the center of the area (room/location). </p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >| Locations have no real boundaries - they are infinite. (That means: the real content is always close to the center. There is nothing to find on the edges!)</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >| The only right way to navigate is finding and following &quot;the guides&quot;. Some are actual signposts, some are text hints, some are the paths that creatures follow, etc. Surprisingly, that kind of navigation is much closer to real life, than anything.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>WARNING II:</i> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>NO GAMEPAD SUPPORT!</strong> You have to click rather quickly and with a high precision too. Keyboard and mouse is the only comfortable (and well tested) way to play it. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>WARNING III:</i></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >For more info about the game - read the manual. You can find it right on this page in the column below the banner <i>&gt;&gt;&gt;</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2384020/extras/c40411d829092f3641b7cbad93e4c558.avif?t=1749786548\" /></span></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2384020/extras/aa5e9eb451fb97f592759f5229e06a62.avif?t=1749786548\" /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>OVERVIEW:</i></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bioysque is a retro-style Action RPG in a dark bio-horror environment, both sci-fi and fantasy motives. You are always alone and they are always many. Fight surreal creatures, get experience, explore and gather upgrades - get stronger before the next big Boss fight, learn the truth. Win and be rewarded.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>DEVELOPER'S MESSAGE:</i></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I never intended to make this game. But I saw it in a dream, so I had to make it! For some strange reason, that's pretty rare for me. I have seen about 3 dreams in my whole life (or more likely, those are all I remember). I had to try at least. (<strong><i>time skip here</i></strong>) And here it is. I actually made the game I saw in a dream. What could be more surreal than that?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2384020/extras/5fa19cc563e1e69b035bf57057b282b4.avif?t=1749786548\" /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>3 MOST IMPORTANT FEATURES:</i></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rare - <i>forgotten/unknown</i> - Biopunk Sci-Fi/Fantasy setting; short but multi-layered story</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unique &lt;direct click&gt; battle system: no time wasted! Hit whatever you see wherever it is!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Mostly Wall-less level design and portal-based world. <i>*more about it in the section below...</i></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2384020/extras/ba675d8106948968ebbac7a9dc99a757.webp?t=1749786548\" /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>WARNING I:</i></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Exploration done differently, and I think it's preferable to know, before you try the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2384020/extras/aded8ff0726c28639613ce4910842132.avif?t=1749786548\" /></span></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >| Most rooms/locations are connected via portals. </p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >| You always start in the center of the area (room/location). </p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >| Locations have no real boundaries - they are infinite. (That means: the real content is always close to the center. There is nothing to find on the edges!)</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >| The only right way to navigate is finding and following &quot;the guides&quot;. Some are actual signposts, some are text hints, some are the paths that creatures follow, etc. Surprisingly, that kind of navigation is much closer to real life, than anything.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>WARNING II:</i> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>NO GAMEPAD SUPPORT!</strong> You have to click rather quickly and with a high precision too. Keyboard and mouse is the only comfortable (and well tested) way to play it. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>WARNING III:</i></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >For more info about the game - read the manual. You can find it right on this page in the column below the banner <i>&gt;&gt;&gt;</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2384020/extras/c40411d829092f3641b7cbad93e4c558.avif?t=1749786548\" /></span></p>",
